    `Father, I receive today the story I am living inside — the one story of the Bible, the recovery operation that You have been running since the moment the garden was lost and You called out where are you in the cool of the evening. I am not an isolated individual navigating a random life. I am a person living inside the most important story ever told — the story of a God who made a garden for communion, lost it in catastrophe, and has been recovering it ever since at infinite cost. Let me live today with the perspective of the full story — from the garden of Genesis to the garden-city of Revelation. Let the new Jerusalem be the fixed point on the horizon that gives meaning to everything between Eden and the end. And let the tree of life that the leaves of the nations will be healed by be the destination that orients every step I take in the direction of the One who planted the first garden because He wanted to walk with me in it. You are still walking. I am no longer hiding.`
