    `Father, I receive today the righteousness that is not my own — the righteousness of Christ, credited to my account through faith, making me before You not merely forgiven but righteous. Not righteous in the performance sense — the achieved, maintained, vulnerable-to-failure righteousness of my own effort. Righteous in the imputed sense — clothed in the perfect righteousness of the One who perfectly fulfilled every requirement of the law and whose standing before You is now my standing through union with Him. Let this truth change how I approach You today. Not the anxious petition of someone whose standing depends on how well the week has gone. The bold, settled, grateful approach of someone who knows that the standing they have is not their own and therefore cannot be lost by anything they do or fail to do. I am found in Him. Not having a righteousness of my own. The righteousness that comes from God on the basis of faith. It is enough. It is more than enough. It is everything.`
